      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "'Females: 15 persons.' The tail of the red-ink (原朱) head-note on Kishiwada's shrine-family (社家) count, which begins in the top margin of the facing page lower_p058_left (printed 93) as （原朱）社家十七戸 人員五十人 男子三十五人. 35 males + 15 females = the 50 persons stated there -- the arithmetic is what proves this fragment is Kishiwada's, not Kikuma's, even though it sits directly above Kikuma's page."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "社家内女子（岸和田藩分・頭注）"
